" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"host-a-web-game\">Host a web game<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#host-a-web-game\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>Upload a finished HTML5 game as a <code>.zip</code> and get a link people can play in the browser, an\n<code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code> embed and a <code>&lt;verse-viewer&gt;</code> tag. Games run on their own site, <strong>play.ctruh.io</strong>, so a\ngame can never read your Verse account.</p>\n<h2 id=\"upload\">Upload<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#upload\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<ol><li>Studio → <strong>Web games → Host a game</strong> (or drop a <code>.zip</code> on the upload page).</li><li>Wait for the checks to finish. You get:\n<ul><li>a player page: <code>https://verse.ctruh.com/play/&lt;id&gt;</code>;</li><li>the game itself: <code>https://play.ctruh.io/g/&lt;id&gt;/</code>;</li><li>copy-paste embed code.</li></ul></li><li>Optional: add a cover image (PNG, JPG or WebP up to 3 MB), set an orientation, or make the game private and share it with a code.</li></ol>\n<p>To update a game keep the same link: <strong>Replace build</strong> and upload the new zip.</p>\n<h2 id=\"embed-it\">Embed it<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#embed-it\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"html\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-html\">&lt;script type=&quot;module&quot; src=&quot;https://verse.ctruh.com/sdk/verse-viewer.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;verse-viewer type=&quot;game&quot; src=&quot;YOUR_GAME_ID&quot;&gt;&lt;/verse-viewer&gt;</code></pre></div>\n<p>or an <code>&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://play.ctruh.io/g/YOUR_GAME_ID/&quot; allowfullscreen&gt;</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-works\">What works<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#what-works\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Anything that is a static web build: three.js, Babylon, Phaser, plain canvas, Unity WebGL\n(<code>Build/*.loader.js</code>, <code>.framework.js.br</code>, <code>.data.br</code>, <code>.wasm.br</code>), Godot 4 web exports. Compressed\nUnity builds are served with the right headers.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Limit</th><th>Free</th><th>Starter</th><th>Pro</th><th>Scale</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Games</td><td>3</td><td>unlimited</td><td>unlimited</td><td>unlimited</td></tr><tr><td>Zip size</td><td>100 MB</td><td>500 MB</td><td>1 GB</td><td>2 GB</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The zip may hold up to 4,000 files and may unpack to at most five times your plan&#39;s size. Symlinks,\nabsolute or <code>..</code> paths and password-protected zips are refused. Server-side scripts (<code>.php</code>, <code>.py</code>,\n<code>.sh</code>, <code>.exe</code>), hidden files and <code>__MACOSX</code> folders are dropped, and the upload tells you how many.</p>\n<h2 id=\"good-to-know\">Good to know<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#good-to-know\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li>A game is somebody&#39;s code. It runs on <code>play.ctruh.io</code> with its own storage (saves in localStorage and IndexedDB work) and none of your Verse cookies.</li><li>Games on <code>play.ctruh.io</code> are isolated so multi-threaded Unity and Godot builds work when the game is opened there. A game embedded on another site is isolated only if that site is too; single-threaded builds work anywhere.</li><li>Export with Brotli or gzip compression, as Unity does. Uncompressed <code>.wasm</code> is served as is.</li><li>Very old Unity builds (<code>.unityweb</code>, Unity 2019 and earlier) are served as plain files.</li></ul>\n<p>API: <code>POST /v1/games</code> with the zip as the body. See the <a href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-api-reference\">API reference</a>.</p></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/host-a-web-game\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#upload\" id=\"lnk-upload\">Upload</a><a href=\"#embed-it\" id=\"lnk-embed-it\">Embed it</a><a href=\"#what-works\" id=\"lnk-what-works\">What works</a><a href=\"#good-to-know\" id=\"lnk-good-to-know\">Good to know</a></aside></section>"}